Z||000002||terryk||05-11-2001||12:38 AM||||Yes and no. You can, but the cost will exceed the cost of getting one from a wrecker in the end. The intake, injectors, TB, accessory brackets, blower, fuel rail, wiring, ECM, not to mention the crank and balance/pulley. It just keeps adding up.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCFIERO||05-11-2001||07:31 AM||||Terry,<P>So it is not just an easy switch to a SC.  I was hoping it was a simple intake removal and insert the SC intake.  What else could I do to this motor to get mor horses||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||05-11-2001||12:09 PM||||Turbo or NOS, or the standard balance/port/polish, cam, mill the heads to about 9.5:1.<P>After that, not much.<P>No, the SC doesn't just bolt on. ||||reg||1
